Kimi CLI is not crashing because of a Kimi bug or your repo size. **The repo's own verification tools are killing it.** Every single crash follows the same pattern.

## The Root Cause: Tool Timeout Cascade

Kimi CLI has a **hard 60-second shell command timeout**. Your verification tools exceed that limit because they run subprocesses **sequentially**, and the chain nests multiple layers deep:

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["bootstrap/auto_onboard.py"] -->|"calls"| B["tools/agent_health_check.py"]
    A -->|"calls"| C["tools/onboard_agent.py"]
    A -->|"calls"| D["tools/verify_all.py"]
    D -->|"calls sequentially"| E["10 subprocess checks"]
    E -->|"includes"| F["standards_check.py --verify"]
    F -->|"runs sequentially"| G["60 enforcement commands"]
    G -->|"each spawns"| H["python3 subprocess with 60s timeout"]
    
    style F fill:#fff,stroke:#f00,stroke-width:3px
    style G fill:#fff,stroke:#f00,stroke-width:3px
```

**`standards_check.py --verify`** is the primary killer. It runs **60 enforcement commands sequentially**, each with a 60s subprocess timeout. Many of these commands themselves spawn Python processes (e.g., `python3 audit/popperian_audit.py 2>&1 | tail -3`). Total wall time: easily 5-10 minutes. [8-cite-0](#8-cite-0) 

**`verify_all.py`** runs 10 checks sequentially, including `_check_standards()` which calls `standards_check.py --verify`. Even with `--skip-tests --skip-merkle`, it still runs 8 checks including the standards check. Total wall time: easily >120s. [8-cite-1](#8-cite-1) 

**`auto_onboard.py`** chains health_check + onboard_agent + verify_all. It inherits all the slowness.

